course: dictionary
lesson: 14815
title: Qualified: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. The clues around the word are its context. «Mum is a qualified nurse, so she can give medicine at the clinic.» The job nurse and the word medicine tell you that qualified means she has passed the exams and training for this job.
explain: «The swimmer has qualified for the final.» Here there is no job and no exam. The clue is final, the last part of a competition. In sport, qualified means a swimmer has won a place in the next part of the competition.
explain: The word can also mean having the right skills or knowledge to do something. «Only qualified people should fix the gas pipes, because it is dangerous.» The clue is dangerous, so qualified means knowing how to do it safely. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking if it still makes sense.
explain: In formal writing, qualified can mean limited, not complete. «Her approval was qualified, so she agreed only in part.» The clue is only in part, so qualified means not full agreement.
fact: Qualified means having passed the exams or training needed to do a job.
fact: Qualified also means having the right skills or knowledge to do something.
fact: In sport, qualified means having won a place in the next part of a competition.
fact: In formal writing, «qualified approval» means approval that is limited, not complete.
fact: «Fully qualified» means every exam and training needed for the job has been completed.
exercise: «Dad is a qualified electrician, so he can fix the wiring.» What does qualified mean here? | *Covered in paint | Quickly finished | Passed the training needed for the job | Very tired after a long day
exercise: «The swimmer has qualified for the national final.» What does qualified mean? | Has lost every race | Has learned to swim in the sea | Has a new swimming hat | *Has won a place in the next part of the competition
exercise: What does qualified mean in «Her approval was qualified, so she agreed only in part»? | *Only partly, not complete | Very loud | Made of gold | Fully finished
test: «Kai wants to be a doctor, so he must be fully qualified before he can work.» What does fully qualified mean? | *Has passed all the exams and training needed for the job | Owns a stethoscope | Has finished school for the day
test: Which sentence uses qualified to mean having the right skills to do something? | «The qualified box was heavy.» | *«Only qualified people should fix the gas pipes.» | «The children qualified for the bus.» | «The team has qualified for the final.»
exam: What does qualified mean in «The paramedic is qualified to give first aid»? | Tired and sleepy | Finished with a medal | Very fast | *Trained and allowed to do the job
